      "classes": "1: NO MATCH -- A temperature setpoint is not an air quality sensor.\n2: NO MATCH -- A temperature setpoint is not a condensing unit.\n3: NO MATCH -- A temperature setpoint is not a heat exchanger.\n4: NO MATCH -- A temperature setpoint is not a humidifier.\n5: NO MATCH -- A temperature setpoint is not an isolation valve.\n6: NO MATCH -- A temperature setpoint is not a dry cooler.",
      "relationships": "1: MATCH 13 -- An AHU has a fan as a part.\n2: MATCH 14 -- An AHU has a filter as a part.\n3: MATCH 15 -- An AHU has a damper as a part.\n4: MATCH 16 -- An AHU has a cooling valve as a part.\n5: MATCH 17 -- An AHU has a heating valve as a part.\n6: MATCH 18 -- An AHU has an economizer as a part.\n7: MATCH 8 -- Both link the AHU to its air temperature sensor.\n8: MATCH 19 -- Both link the AHU to its CO2 sensor.\n9: MATCH 9 -- Both link the AHU to its air temperature setpoint.\n10: MATCH 10 -- Both link the AHU to its cooling temperature setpoint.\n11: MATCH 11 -- Both link the AHU to its heating temperature setpoint.\n12: MATCH 12 -- Both link the AHU to its temperature deadband setpoint.\n13: MATCH 6 -- Both link the thermostat to its temperature sensor.\n14: MATCH 7 -- Both link the thermostat to its temperature setpoint.\n15: MATCH 5 -- Both link the zone to its occupancy sensor.\n16: MATCH 1 -- A building containing a floor expresses the part relationship.\n17: MATCH 2 -- A floor containing a space expresses the part relationship.\n18: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a building to a zone as a part.\n19: MATCH 20 -- Both link the AHU to its outside air CO2 sensor.\n20: MATCH 21 -- Both link the AHU to its return air CO2 sensor.",
      "properties": "1: MATCH \"temperatureReading\" -- Both denote the measured temperature.\n2: NO MATCH -- A temperature reading is not the sensor's status.\n3: MATCH \"temperatureReading\" -- Both denote the measured air temperature.\n4: MATCH \"concentration\" -- A CO2 sensor's value is its measured concentration.\n5: MATCH \"concentration\" -- Both denote the measured outside-air CO2 concentration.\n6: MATCH \"concentration\" -- Both denote the measured return-air CO2 concentration.\n7: MATCH \"targetTemperature\" -- Both denote the temperature setpoint value.\n8: MATCH \"targetTemperature\" -- Both denote the air-temperature setpoint value.\n9: MATCH \"targetTemperature\" -- Both denote the cooling-temperature setpoint value.\n10: MATCH \"targetTemperature\" -- Both denote the heating-temperature setpoint value.\n11: MATCH \"temperatureDifference\" -- A temperature deadband setpoint specifies a temperature difference.\n12: NO MATCH -- An occupancy reading does not clearly specify the occupied boolean.\n13: MATCH \"insideOutsideDifference\" -- Both denote the measured CO2 differential.\n14: MATCH \"temperatureReading\" -- Both denote the measured water temperature.",
